WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.400
Good Morning Hank it's Thursday

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.940
It's the Fourth day of Pizza-mas

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.600
and I have just one thing to say.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:05.940
"YYAAAAAaaaAAA!"

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:06.440
"YYAAAAAAAA!"

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:07.900
"AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHHHHHHH!"

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.720
"YAAAAAAAAA!"

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.300
Thank you for including this in your video, Hank,

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.960
because I actually think about this man a lot.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.300
I call him Cheez Doodles Guy,

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.060
and my current number one goal in life,

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:21.640
is to someday be as excited about something as Cheez Doodles guy is about Cheez Doodles.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:25.000
But it's a weird facet of human brains that some things cause that joyful excitement,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.200
and others don't.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.360
Like today, the World Health Organization announced that maternal death over the last 25 years

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.400
has fallen 44% worldwide.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:38.060
This is amazing news, arguably even better news than discovering Cheez Doodles in Antarctica.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:41.880
And yet while I am encouraged by this news, I am not Cheez Doodles Guy excited about it,

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.440
which is so weird. Humans are so weird.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.180
But anyway, Hank, this video isn't about Cheez Doodles. It's Thursday!

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.740
It's Question Thursday, the day that I answer real questions from real NerdFighters.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:50.720
Let's get right to it.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.180
Why did you shave your beard? I just started to like it!

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.700
Mostly for the mustache joke, but also it was kinda itchy.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:59.120
Who is your least favorite Beatle, and what is your least favorite color?

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.080
Ringo Silver. That's a funny name.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:04.700
I feel like Ringo Silver would have a mustache, and maybe a curious hat,

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.760
and a pet monkey and together they would solve crimes.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:10.480
Hey, how many Pizza John shirts can you wear at the same time?

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.140
Oh, I can wear all of them and fairly comfortably as it turns out.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.400
Nonetheless, I think I'm gonna stick with just the one for now.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.000
Do you know anymore dad jokes?

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.620
I feel like dad jokes aren't something you know so much as they're something you are.

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:22.180
Like every time I'm putting away the dishes,

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.940
I always say, "Tupperware, tupperware, tupper-here!"

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.120
And then I go to the tupperware drawer,

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.700
And then Sarah looks at me with just...

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:32.540
absolute disgust.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:33.700
Pizza, or-

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.780
Pizza! It's always pizza!

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.240
How do you feel about vegetables?

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:38.380
They're great on pizza!

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.100
What should I get my boyfriend for Christmas?

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.820
Might I recommend Pizza John shoelaces,

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:45.520
the perfect gift for someone who has everything,

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:49.600
except for a way to keep their shoes on, available only during Pizzamas,

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:51.100
at dftba.com.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.680
What's your opinion on licorice?

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:53.800
Strongly in favor!

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.160
How do you become well-read?

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:58.320
I don't know. I mostly read books that are recommended to me by people that I trust,

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.580
but I will give you a book recommendation.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:04.760
This amazing, weird, sci-fi book, Midnight Robber, I love it.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:07.820
Would you consider getting a real tattoo, now that you've gotten a fake one?

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:11.140
Well, I don't think my tattoo is fake. It was just made with water instead of ink.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:13.940
So it's not technically visible, but it's still real.

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:16.240
I would consider getting more invisible tattoos.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:17.540
What do you think about ducks?

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:20.280
Well I spent an inordinate amount of time thinking about what happens to them

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:22.620
when the pond freezes over in winter, I'll tell you that.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.200
How do you become okay with being truly alone?

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.380
Okay, so I would argue that you're both never and always truly alone.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:32.980
Like you're always truly alone in the sense that no one can ever fully comprehend your experience,

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.560
or live inside your consciousness.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.240
But you're also never truly alone,

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.780
because just like by virtue of living or having left that comment,

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:42.640
you're part of this massive, interconnected web of life on earth.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.160
And that web is grateful to have you here

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:49.500
And when I can remember that, it helps give me the energy to connect more meaningfully with other people,

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.680
whether it's online or in real life.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:56.600
And in turn that makes me more aware of this big web that I'm part of, which makes me feel less alone.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.460
What is the opposite of guacamole?

00:02:58.460 --> 00:02:59.240
Elomacaug.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:02.940
In 50 years, what country do you think will be the world's biggest superpower?

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.860
In general, I think that nation-states will be slightly less important than they are now,

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:07.400
but I'm gonna say, India.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.940
What's your favorite research chemical?

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:10.200
What am I? Walter White?

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.840
What should I get my girlfriend for our three-year anniversary?

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.400
Let me answer your question with a question.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.980
Does your girlfriend enjoy drinking liquids?

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:20.240
Because if so, she might enjoy this Pizza John travel mug,

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:23.860
available for preorder only during Pizzamas at dftba.com

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:25.980
How do I deal with the death of my cactus?

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:30.960
Well, things will get easier with time, but I think for a while at least, you're gonna feel a little prickly.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.880
I'm sorry, I hate myself.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.660
Do you still have any leftover Halloween candy?

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:38.200
If you mean, does your two-year-old daughter still have some leftover Halloween candy,

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.900
and you eat it occasionally because she's two, and won't notice,

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:41.980
then yes.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:44.460
Hank, happy Pizzamas! Yaaaaaah!

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:44.980
Nah.

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:48.160
You know, I'm excited about Pizzamas, I'm just not that excited.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:49.260
I'll see you tomorrow.

